  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRANSHUMANCE AND CONSERVATION AT A CROSSROADS - COMPARATIVE INVESTIGATION ACROSS WEST-CENTRAL AFRICAN LANDSCAPES OF GLOBAL BIODIVERSITY SIGNIFICANCE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Specific activities include (1) conducting an.institutional analysis of transhumance governance in.southern Chad and CAR in relation to the WAP.conservation complex; (2) producing a transhumant.mobility analysis in the Chadian regions of Moyen-Chari.and Salamat; and (3) conducting geospatial analysis of.pastoral resource distribution and connectivity across.southern Chad and CAR. The funding source is a 632(b).transfer from USAID; transfer responsibilities include.implementation of the Central Africa Regional Program.for the Environment (CARPE).</narrative>
  </description>
